# Six-revolute spatial manipulator: an "elbow manipulator" with spherical
# wrist -- the standard serial-arm example of the robotics texts (Spong
# ch. 3, Craig ch. 3). Maximally serial: every body's parent is the previous
# body, so the joint-space inertia matrix H is fully dense. The axes mix
# z, y, and x so the motion is fully three-dimensional.

gravity 0 0 -9.81

body                    # 0: waist column, rotates about vertical
parent -1
joint revolute z
tree 0 0 0.5
mass 10
cg 0 0 0.25
inertia 0.23 0.23 0.05 0 0 0

body                    # 1: upper arm, shoulder pitch
parent 0
joint revolute y
tree 0 0 0.3
mass 5
cg 0.2 0 0
inertia 0.01 0.07 0.07 0 0 0

body                    # 2: forearm, elbow pitch
parent 1
joint revolute y
tree 0.4 0 0
mass 3
cg 0.2 0 0
inertia 0.01 0.04 0.04 0 0 0

body                    # 3: wrist roll
parent 2
joint revolute z
tree 0.4 0 0
mass 1
cg 0.05 0 0
inertia 0.005 0.005 0.002 0 0 0

body                    # 4: wrist pitch
parent 3
joint revolute y
tree 0.1 0 0
mass 0.8
cg 0.04 0 0
inertia 0.004 0.004 0.002 0 0 0

body                    # 5: wrist yaw / tool plate; external force here
parent 4
joint revolute x
tree 0.1 0 0
mass 0.5
cg 0.03 0 0
inertia 0.002 0.003 0.003 0 0 0
fext 1
